---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCountries, getInstitutions, getSources, getEvidence } from '../../lib/data';
import { url, repoTree, repoFile, REPO_URL } from '../../lib/url';
const counts = { countries: getCountries().length, institutions: getInstitutions().length, sources: getSources().length, evidence: getEvidence().length };
---
<Base title="Open data" description="Download Academic Safeguard Europe research data as YAML or JSON." crumbs={[{ label: 'Open data' }]}>
  <div class="container prose">
    <h1>Open data</h1>
    <p class="lede">All research data is public and licensed under CC BY 4.0. The canonical data is the YAML in the repository. The JSON files below are generated from it at every build.</p>

    <h2>JSON exports</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="exports-cap">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden" id="exports-cap">JSON exports</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Dataset</th><th scope="col">Records</th><th scope="col">Download</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Countries (all 27 Member States)</th><td>{counts.countries}</td><td><a href={url('/data/countries.json')}>countries.json</a></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Institutions</th><td>{counts.institutions}</td><td><a href={url('/data/institutions.json')}>institutions.json</a></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Sources</th><td>{counts.sources}</td><td><a href={url('/data/sources.json')}>sources.json</a></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Evidence Library</th><td>{counts.evidence}</td><td><a href={url('/data/evidence-library.json')}>evidence-library.json</a></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Rubric</th><td>12 safeguards</td><td><a href={url('/data/rubric.json')}>rubric.json</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Repository data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={repoTree('data/countries')}><code>data/countries/</code></a>: one file per Member State</li>
      <li><a href={repoTree('data/institutions')}><code>data/institutions/</code></a>: one folder per country</li>
      <li><a href={repoTree('data/sources')}><code>data/sources/</code></a>: the source register</li>
      <li><a href={repoFile('methodology/scoring-rubric.yml')}><code>methodology/scoring-rubric.yml</code></a>: safeguard definitions</li>
      <li><a href={repoTree('research')}><code>research/</code></a>: research dossiers, including verification notes</li>
      <li><a href={repoFile('docs/data-model.md')}><code>docs/data-model.md</code></a>: field definitions</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Using the data responsibly</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep <code>NR</code>, <code>?</code> and <code>0</code> distinct. Don't convert them to numbers for averaging.</li>
      <li>Check each finding's <code>verification</code> field. <code>needs_review</code> findings are provisional and have not been verified by a human reviewer. Each JSON file also carries a <code>verification_summary</code> and <code>caveats</code>.</li>
      <li>Don't build overall rankings from these results. The methodology is not designed for aggregation.</li>
      <li>Cite the methodology version and the date you downloaded the data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Suggested citation: <em>Academic Safeguard Europe, research data (methodology v0.1), {REPO_URL}, accessed [date]. CC BY 4.0.</em></p>
  </div>
</Base>
